# Extra holidays, and exceptions to the built-in ones.
#
# You do NOT need this file. Report Tracker already skips weekends plus nine
# holidays every year, worked out automatically so they never need updating:
#
#     New Year's Day             1 January
#     Martin Luther King Day     third Monday in January
#     Memorial Day               last Monday in May
#     Independence Day           4 July
#     Labor Day                  first Monday in September
#     Thanksgiving Day           fourth Thursday in November
#     Friday after Thanksgiving  the day after
#     Christmas Eve              24 December
#     Christmas Day              25 December
#
# A holiday falling on a Saturday is taken the Friday before, and one falling on
# a Sunday the Monday after, matching normal US practice.
#
# Christmas Eve and Christmas Day would otherwise land on the same day in about
# one year in three. Two days are always granted: in 2027 they fall on Thursday
# 23 and Friday 24 December, and in 2028 on Monday 25 and Tuesday 26 December.
#
# Copy this file to holidays.txt next to the app only if you want to change any
# of that.
#
# ADD a day off: one date per line, YYYY-MM-DD. For example, if your site also
# closes the day before Independence Day in 2026:
# 2026-07-02
#
# REMOVE a built-in holiday your site does not observe: put a minus in front.
# For example, if you work the Friday after Thanksgiving in 2026:
# -2026-11-27
#
# Good Friday is NOT observed by default. If your site does close, add the date
# each year, since it moves with Easter:
# 2026-04-03
# 2027-03-26
# 2028-04-14
#
# Anything after a "#" is ignored, and a line that does not parse costs only that
# one line rather than the whole file.
